course: dictionary
lesson: 6076
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Ruby left a message for her mum» means words left for someone to read or hear. «What is the message of the story?» means something quite different: the big idea the story wants to teach.
explain: Look at the words around the word. Messages sent on a phone are texts, so when you see «phone» or «send», message probably means a text or a note. Then ask: which meaning fits, and does it still make sense when you put it into the sentence?
explain: Message can also be a verb in informal speech, meaning to send someone a text. «I will message you later» means I will send you a text later. The same pattern works for messaged and messaging.
fact: A message is a piece of information sent or left for another person, in words, writing or on a phone.
fact: A text message, email or chat note sent on a phone or computer is also a message.
fact: The message of a story is its main idea or lesson, as in «What is the message of the story?»
fact: «Messages can be saved, shared and misunderstood, so you never send what you would not say face to face.»
fact: Informal: to message someone means to send them a text message.
exercise: In «Ruby... looked at his games and messages», what does messages mean? | Packets of data cut into small pieces | Money paid for a service | *Texts and chat notes sent to him | Lessons from a story
exercise: «What is the message of the story?» What does message mean in this question? | Words left on a voicemail | *The main lesson or big idea | A text sent on a phone
exercise: «I will message you later.» What does message mean in this sentence? | To leave a note on a door | To read a story aloud | To pay for something | *To send someone a text
test: «Nerves carry messages from the brain to the body.» What does message mean here? | The main idea of a story | A loud shout | *Signals of information sent along a path | A written letter from a friend
test: A stranger sends you a mean or scary message. What is the best thing to do? | Reply angrily to the stranger | Share it with your friends | *Do not answer it and tell an adult | Send a photo back to them
exam: «A stranger began sending her messages.» What does messages mean here? | Lessons from a book | Packets of data cut into small pieces | Pictures painted on a wall | *Texts or notes sent to her by someone
